Three fixes, all from user reports

• New action "Block the key (do nothing)" — for side keys that report as F1/F2, which made browsers open a tab. Leaving a key on "No action" passes it through; this swallows it.
• New action "Let the app handle this key" — use it in an app profile for readers that use the key themselves. "No action" in a profile inherits the global mapping, so it could not express this.
• Side keys that report as "unknown" can now be told apart.
